declarations.description:
Cancel only a durable process created by this runtime. Ownership is verified from stored unit/job metadata; arbitrary PID signalling is not exposed. This tool is part of plugin `h`.

MCP server instructions: Filesystem tools. File lines render as `N:hh|content`; `N:hh` is the line id edit tools target, and edit results are diffs with fresh ids, so edits chain without re-viewing files. Reuse returned content and ids; read complete relevant blocks, then act on them. Each response costs a round trip: first decide what you need next, then request every call that doesn't depend on another's result in that one response.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__h_process_cancel(args: {
  // Grace period before the fallback backend sends SIGKILL, capped at 30 seconds.
  grace_seconds?: number;
  host: string;
  job_id: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Page retained durable job metadata with an optional configured-host filter, opaque snapshot cursor and independent page limit of 1..128. Every response is bounded to 64 KiB. Continue next_cursor until null; inventory_complete is true only on the last page. A fresh first page observes current metadata. Continuations refer to that observation and may be invalidated by source changes, controller restart or bounded snapshot-cache expiry; start a new first page when refused. No job is started, stopped or replayed. Use process_status for authoritative live status. This tool is part of plugin `h`.

